course: dictionary
lesson: 9868
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To choose the right one, look at the words around it, which are its context. «The solar system has eight planets.» Here system means a group of parts that work together as a whole.
explain: «A fair turn-taking system gives everyone a go, the same length of time.» Here system means a planned way of doing something. Ask yourself: does the sentence need a group, a plan, or a set of rules?
explain: Check your choice by swapping your meaning into the sentence. «The immune system fights germs» makes sense if system means a group of parts working together, so that is the right meaning here.
fact: A system is a group of parts that work together as a whole.
fact: «Solar system» means the Sun and the planets that travel around it.
fact: «Immune system» means the body's defence against illness.
fact: A system can also be a planned way of doing something, such as «a good system» for tidying up.
fact: The «metric system» measures length, mass and volume in metres, grams and litres.
exercise: In «the solar system», what does system mean? | A plan for tidying the classroom | A computer with its programs | The Sun and the planets that travel around it | *A group of parts working as a whole
exercise: «A fair turn-taking system gives everyone a go.» What does system mean here? | The Sun and the planets | A group of parts working as a whole | A computer | *A planned way of doing something
exercise: «The metric system» measures length, mass and volume. Which units belong to it? | *Metres, grams and litres | Feet and pounds | Days, hours and minutes | Red, blue and green
test: In «a computer system», what does system mean? | *A computer with its programs | A plan for tidying up | A set of rules for a school | The Sun and the planets
test: Jayden says system only means planets. Is he right? | Yes, and it also means a computer | *No, it has several meanings, such as a planned way of doing something | Yes, it only means planets | No, it means happy
exam: Which sentence uses system to mean a set of rules or ideas? | My computer system has a slow program | The Sun is at the centre of the solar system | I need a good system for tidying my desk | *The number system is based on ten
